Reason (TD-29, design review architect-review-d3 S9; Nam 2026-11-12: "TD-29 patch only (Recommended)"):
the project template has no .claude/settings.json. A project made by `pls init` gets this file (init copies every
file of templates/project/), so the agent may run `python pls.py …` without a prompt each time, and cannot read the
operator's `.pls/` (keys, passwords, connections), release payloads / rollbacks / live copies or test results, nor
edit gate records and the files pls writes in releases/ (template CLAUDE.md hard rule 7), nor push.
Path syntax follows the framework's own .claude/settings.json ("/x" = from the project root, "//x" = absolute).
Not verified here: the exact matching of these rules by Claude Code (check once in a new project: a Read of
.pls/connections.json and of a payload is refused; `python pls.py lint` runs without a prompt).
The patch also adds the file to docs/architecture.md §3.2 (the layout test requires it; suite 501 OK with the patch on 1f8ead4).
Existing projects are not changed (copy the file by hand). bootstrap-log.json exists only after AU3 (committed 2d818e4).
Apply: git apply plans/2026-11-13-td-29-template-claude-settings/proposed-templates-project-claude-settings.json.patch

diff --git a/templates/project/.claude/settings.json b/templates/project/.claude/settings.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e630973
--- /dev/null
+++ b/templates/project/.claude/settings.json
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+{
+  "permissions": {
+    "allow": [
+      "Bash(python pls.py *)",
+      "Bash(py pls.py *)"
+    ],
+    "deny": [
+      "Read(//**/.pls/**)",
+      "Edit(//**/.pls/**)",
+      "Read(/releases/*/payload*.json)",
+      "Read(/releases/*/rollback*.json)",
+      "Read(/releases/*/live-*.json)",
+      "Read(/tests/results/**)",
+      "Edit(/gates/**)",
+      "Edit(/releases/*/plan.json)",
+      "Edit(/releases/*/bootstrap.json)",
+      "Edit(/releases/*/bootstrap-log.json)",
+      "Edit(/releases/*/apply-log.json)",
+      "Edit(/releases/*/payload*.json)",
+      "Edit(/releases/*/rollback*.json)",
+      "Bash(git push)",
+      "Bash(git push *)"
+    ]
+  }
+}
